{=============================================================================
  Combined gas-steam cycle (Brayton topping cycle + Rankine bottoming cycle)
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0052
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Exercise of the ULiege course "Thermodynamique appliquee" (2022-2023),
  repetition 7, exercise 5. The upper cycle is a gas turbine (Brayton) cycle
  whose exhaust gases heat the steam of a simple Rankine cycle in a heat
  exchanger (combined gas-steam cycle). The model computes the steam-to-gas
  flow ratio in the heat exchanger and the thermal efficiency of the combined
  cycle.

  The gas cycle is on air, assumed to be a perfect gas (as in the original,
  which used the EES humid-air pseudo-fluid "Air_ha" with no humidity, i.e. dry
  air); the steam cycle is on water. All the components are analysed as
  isobaric or as isentropic machines, with a constant isentropic efficiency;
  no pressure loss, no combustion chemistry and no flow rate are given by the
  statement. The steam-to-gas flow ratio is obtained from the energy balance of
  the heat exchanger and the cycle efficiency from the sum of the machine
  powers over the heat released by the topping cycle.

  Inputs : T_TGV[1], T_TGV[3], T_TGV[5], eta_is_cp, eta_is_turb,
           P_TGV[1], P_TGV[2]/P_TGV[1], P[2], P[4], T[3], x[1]
  Outputs: Ratio_ORC_TGV (steam flow rate / gas flow rate), n_th (thermal
           efficiency of the combined cycle)
  Units  : SI - temperatures in degC, pressures in Pa, energies in J
           (converted by hand from K/kPa/kJ, original values kept in comments)
  Source : ULiege course "Thermodynamique appliquee", 2022-2023, repetition 7,
           exercise 5 (EES file R07_E05_2022.EES) - see README.md
=============================================================================}

"Data"
T_TGV[1] = 26.85 [C]    "air inlet temperature of the gas cycle (300 K in the original)"
T_TGV[3] = 1026.85 [C]  "air inlet temperature of the gas turbine (1300 K in the original)"
T_TGV[5] = 176.85 [C]   "exhaust gas temperature at the outlet of the heat exchanger (450 K in the original)"
eta_is_cp = 0.8         "isentropic efficiency of the gas compressor [-]"
eta_is_turb = 0.85      "isentropic efficiency of the gas turbine [-]"
P_TGV[1] = 1E5 [Pa]     "ambient pressure, as in the original the Brayton cycle takes in and rejects air at ambient pressure (100 kPa in the original)"
P_TGV[2]/P_TGV[1] = 8   "compressor pressure ratio of the Brayton cycle [-]"
P[2] = 7E6 [Pa]         "steam pressure at the turbine inlet of the Rankine cycle (7000 kPa in the original)"
P[4] = 5E3 [Pa]         "condenser pressure of the Rankine cycle (5 kPa in the original)"
T[3] = 500 [C]          "steam temperature at the turbine inlet of the Rankine cycle (773.15 K, i.e. 500 C, in the original)"
x[1] = 0                "assumption of the original, in the absence of data: saturated liquid at the pump inlet, which the T-s diagram of the statement confirms"

"!Pressures"
P_TGV[5] = P_TGV[1]     "exhaust gas rejected at ambient pressure"
P_TGV[5] = P_TGV[4]     "heat exchanger: isobaric"
P_TGV[3] = P_TGV[2]     "boiler: isobaric"
P[2] = P[3]             "heat exchanger: isobaric"
P[4] = P[1]             "condenser: isobaric (as in the original)"

"!1: gas turbine cycle (TGV)"
"Stations: 1 compressor inlet, 2 compressor outlet, 3 turbine inlet,
 4 turbine outlet, 5 outlet of the heat exchanger (exhaust gases)."
s_TGV[1] = entropy(Air,T=T_TGV[1],P=P_TGV[1])
h_TGV[1] = enthalpy(Air,T=T_TGV[1],P=P_TGV[1])
h_TGV_2_is = enthalpy(Air,s=s_TGV[1],P=P_TGV[2])   "isentropic compressor outlet state"
eta_is_cp = (h_TGV_2_is-h_TGV[1])/(h_TGV[2]-h_TGV[1])   "by definition, as in the original"
s_TGV[3] = entropy(Air,T=T_TGV[3],P=P_TGV[3])
h_TGV[3] = enthalpy(Air,T=T_TGV[3],P=P_TGV[3])
h_TGV_4_is = enthalpy(Air,s=s_TGV[3],P=P_TGV[4])   "isentropic turbine outlet state"
eta_is_turb = (h_TGV[4]-h_TGV[3])/(h_TGV_4_is-h_TGV[3])   "by definition, as in the original"
T_TGV[4] = temperature(Air,h=h_TGV[4],P=P_TGV[4])
h_TGV[5] = enthalpy(Air,T=T_TGV[5],P=P_TGV[5])

"!2: steam cycle"
"Stations: 1 pump inlet, 2 pump outlet, 3 turbine inlet, 4 turbine outlet.
 The cycle is walked through from the turbine inlet, where the most
 information is available, as in the original."
h[3] = enthalpy(Water,T=T[3],P=P[3])
s[3] = entropy(Water,T=T[3],P=P[3])
s[4] = s[3]   "isentropic turbine, as in the statement"
h[4] = enthalpy(Water,s=s[4],P=P[4])
h[1] = enthalpy(Water,x=x[1],P=P[1])
s[1] = entropy(Water,x=x[1],P=P[1])
s[2] = s[1]   "isentropic pump, as in the statement"
h[2] = enthalpy(Water,s=s[2],P=P[2])

"!Steam-to-gas flow ratio in the heat exchanger"
"The statement gives neither a flow rate nor a power, but the ratio of the
 flow rates follows from the enthalpies: in the heat exchanger,
 m_dot_TGV*(h_TGV[5]-h_TGV[4]) = m_dot_ORC*(h[3]-h[2])"
Ratio_ORC_TGV = abs((h_TGV[5]-h_TGV[4])/(h[3]-h[2]))   "steam flow rate / gas flow rate [-]"

"!Thermal efficiency of the combined cycle"
"Thermal efficiency = useful effect / costly effect. The costly effect is the
 heat released by the topping cycle, Q_TGV_2_3 = m_dot_TGV*(h_TGV[3]-h_TGV[2]).
 The useful effect is the sum of the two turbine powers and of the two
 machine powers absorbed (compressor and pump):
 m_dot_TGV*(h_TGV[4]-h_TGV[3]) + m_dot_TGV*(h_TGV[2]-h_TGV[1])
 + m_dot_ORC*(h[4]-h[3]) + m_dot_ORC*(h[2]-h[1]).
 The flow rates are linked by Ratio_ORC_TGV = m_dot_ORC/m_dot_TGV, so the
 common m_dot_TGV is simplified and the efficiency is computable without any
 flow rate, as in the original."
n_th = abs((h_TGV[4]-h_TGV[3] + h_TGV[2]-h_TGV[1])+Ratio_ORC_TGV*(h[4]-h[3] + h[2]-h[1]))/(h_TGV[3]-h_TGV[2])   "thermal efficiency of the combined cycle [-]"

{State points of the two cycles, for the thermodynamic diagrams. The gas
 cycle: stations 1 (compressor inlet) to 5 (heat-exchanger outlet) in the
 arrays P_TGV[i], T_TGV[i], h_TGV[i], s_TGV[i]; the steam cycle: stations 1
 (pump inlet) to 4 (turbine outlet) in the arrays P[i], T[i], h[i], s[i],
 x[i]. Only the steam cycle can be plotted as a diagram in CoolSolve
 (the working fluid of the gas cycle is an ideal gas,
 CS-FEAT-DIAGRAM-IDEAL); the missing gas state points are computed here.}
T_TGV[2] = temperature(Air,h=h_TGV[2],P=P_TGV[2])
s_TGV[2] = entropy(Air,h=h_TGV[2],P=P_TGV[2])
s_TGV[4] = entropy(Air,h=h_TGV[4],P=P_TGV[4])
s_TGV[5] = entropy(Air,T=T_TGV[5],P=P_TGV[5])
T[1] = temperature(Water,s=s[1],P=P[1])
T[2] = temperature(Water,h=h[2],P=P[2])
T[4] = temperature(Water,h=h[4],P=P[4])
x[4] = quality(Water,h=h[4],P=P[4])
